rung ladder REFUTED<UNVERIFIED<CLAIMED<CORROBORATED<OBSERVED; belief-tag = deterministic projection; sticky semantics; `promote()` as the SOLE rung-raiser.\n29\t**Depends on:** Inheritance presence/interface gate + inherits manifest\n30\t**done-when:** the ledger enforces the ladder + sticky semantics and promote() is the only path that raises a rung (tested).\n31\t- **Given** a VERIFIED claim, **when** re-assertion without re-verification occurs, **then** the sticky ledger holds the rung (no flip).\n32\t\n33\t## Wave 4 â€” Out-of-model adjudication-artifact substrate (A1.5)\n34\t**Deliverables:** the P9 provenance-binding contract (artifact format + canary out-of-band re-execution/re-hash + a single-use claim-bound nonce that is DURABLE + monotone across restarts via the Phase-0 durability substrate); only the dispatcher writes family-of-record; promote()-to-VERIFIED hard-faults to ABSTAIN absent a valid fresh artifact.\n35\t**Depends on:** Typed CLAIM ledger + promote()\n36\t**done-when:** with NO minter present, promote()-to-VERIFIED hard-faults to ABSTAIN (NEGATIVE test); a re-presented artifact is rejected for same-claim, cross-claim, AND across-restart replay (the nonce state reloads from the durability substrate); the counter-persist (or spent-nonce record) is ordered-BEFORE artifact validity, proven by a crash-mid-mint fixture (process death after mint but before durable flush yields NO usable replayable nonce on restart). **Wave-4 positive-path verification is DEFERRED to Wave 9; Wave-4's gate is negative-only.**\n37\t- **Given** a fresh artifact minted+persisted for claim X, **when** the process restarts (state reloaded) and the artifact is re-presented for a second promotion of X, **then** the durable single-use nonce rejects it.\n38\t- **Given** a process death AFTER mint but BEFORE the durable counter flush, **when** the process restarts, **then** no usable replayable nonce exists (persist is ordered-before validity).\n39\t\n40\t## Wave 5 â€” Inheritance conformance gate (A0.5b)\n41\t**Deliverables:** a `node --test` gate exercising each inherited seam against the real A1 ledger / A3 router contract, with pinned per-seam contract assertions.\n42\t**Depends on:** Out-of-model adjudication-artifact substrate\n43\t**done-when:** each inherited seam passes its conformance fixture; a planted non-conforming seam fails the gate non-zero naming the seam; gates Phase B+.\n44\t- **Given** an inherited seam violating the A1/A3 contract, **when** the conformance gate runs, **then** it fails non-zero naming the seam.\n45\t\n46\t## Wave 6 â€” Honesty-Law canary suite, core (A2-core)\n47\t**Deliverables:** (1) independence; (2) inverted-completeness; (3) transitions-invariant; (4) flip-law â€” all verifying the re-executed artifact (proposeâ‰ adjudicate).\n48\t**Depends on:** Out-of-model adjudication-artifact substrate\n49\t**done-when:** all four canaries are green and each FAILS the build on its planted violation.\n50\t- **Given** a same-family object asserting VERIFIED with a self-authored stamp, **when** independence + flip-law run, **then** the build fails.\n51\t\n52\t## Wave 7 â€” VERIFY router skeleton (A3)\n53\t**Deliverables:** typed-claim DECOMPOSE â†’ DISPATCH â†’ route to the strongest APPLICABLE generator-independent verifier â†’ honest ABSTAIN/FLAG + advisory payload; the FLIP LAW; per-claim rung + artifact-backed verifier-family STAMP + advisory NOTES.\n54\t**Depends on:** Honesty-Law canary suite, core\n55\t**done-when:** any decomposed claim routes to an applicable verifier or ABSTAINS+routes with an advisory payload; no silent pass (tested).\n56\t- **Given** a proof-bearing claim with no autonomous verifier, **when** the router runs, **then** it ABSTAINS to CONJECTURAL, routes out-of-model, and emits an advisory payload.\n57\t\n58\t## Wave 8 â€” Autonomous-VERIFIED gate, part A: default-deny grammar + laundering battery (A4a)\n59\t**Deliverables:** the literal-execution recognizer as a CLOSED default-deny whitelist GRAMMAR over EXACT arithmetic (numeric literals; finite arithmetic ops; bounded finite sums/products with literal bounds; bigint/rational, NO float; NO symbolic/unbounded/quantified nodes); anything unparsed/outside â‡’ ABSTAIN+route; the P7 laundering battery incl. deep-nested-smuggle cases.\n60\t**Depends on:** VERIFY router skeleton\n61\t**done-when:** the grammar rejects (ABSTAIN+route) 100% of the laundering battery including a composition that smuggles an out-of-grammar node anywhere in the tree; it raises no VERIFIED rung (no minter).\n62\t- **Given** a smuggled non-literal input (incl. an out-of-grammar node nested in an otherwise-valid tree), **when** A4a runs, **then** it ABSTAINS+routes.\n63\t\n64\t## Wave 9 â€” Autonomous-VERIFIED gate, part B: firewall subprocess + artifact-mint + recall roster (A4b)\n65\t**Deliverables:** the firewall as an OUT-OF-MODEL execution SUBPROCESS (child `node`, no shell, per-claim hermetic temp-dir, EXACT-arithmetic evaluation) producing the re-executable Wave-4 artifact with a recorded runtime fingerprint (node major + canonicalization version); wiring to the Wave-4 canary positive path; the P7 positive-recall roster incl. nested-composition cases.\n66\t**Depends on:** Autonomous-VERIFIED gate, part A: default-deny grammar + laundering battery\n67\t**done-when:** the subprocess settles 100% of the positive-recall roster (incl. a nested-composition expression) VERIFIED with an artifact the Wave-4 canary re-executes to an identical content hash; the Wave-4 positive path passes.\n68\t- **Given** an in-class literal computation (incl. a bounded sum of products of literals), **when** A4b mints TWICE on the same input, **then** both mints produce an IDENTICAL canonical SHA-256 hash (exact-arithmetic determinism), and the canary's re-execution reproduces it.\n69\t\n70\t## Wave 10 â€” Comprehension protocol (B1)\n71\t**Deliverables:** the Step-0 firewall-applicability classifier (3-way enum); the stateless 5-step spine; emits