d Gandalf + researchPrime commission-envelope EMITTERS; the no-inline-reimplementation boundary canary (import-graph + forbidden-symbol).\n90\t**Depends on:** Coverage-stamp canary\n91\t**done-when:** envelopes emit (never dispatch) and the boundary canary fails the build on an inline reimplementation.\n92\t- **Given** an inline researchPrime/Gandalf reimplementation, **when** the boundary canary runs, **then** the build fails (import-graph + forbidden-symbol).\n93\t\n94\t## Wave 14 â€” M1 read-only dispatch shim (B-shim) â€” closes Milestone M1 (comprehension-only preview)\n95\t**Deliverables:** a minimal read-only single-pillar dispatch shim.\n96\t**Depends on:** Commission emitters + no-inline boundary canary\n97\t**done-when:** the shim routes a user request to UNDERSTAND read-only and satisfies the EXACT predicate the Wave-23 no-dispatch canary will later assert: **no commission-id emitted AND no rung-flip on any shim path** (wave-local check; regression-bound by Wave 23).\n98\t- **Given** any shim path, **when** Wave-14's check runs, **then** no commission-id is emitted and no rung is flipped.\n99\t\n100\t## Wave 15 â€” Generation + typed-claim decompose (C1)\n101\t**Deliverables:** a stateless Polya/Schoenfeld GENERATION pass â†’ typed-claim DECOMPOSE into the A1 ledger.\n102\t**Depends on:** M1 read-only dispatch shim\n103\t**done-when:** a new problem yields a candidate decomposed into typed claims, all at UNVERIFIED, in the ledger.\n104\t- **Given** a new problem, **when** C1 runs, **then** every emitted claim is at UNVERIFIED until the router verifies it.\n105\t\n106\t## Wave 16 â€” Claim-type dispatch classifier (C2)\n107\t**Deliverables:** a fail-safe, separate-pass claim-type DISPATCH classifier with conservative escalation to the proof route.\n108\t**Depends on:** Generation + typed-claim decompose\n109\t**done-when:** ambiguous/borderline claims escalate conservatively to the proof route (ABSTAIN+route), never silently to autonomous-VERIFIED (tested)