ve 20 â€” FORMALIZE Lakatosian loop (D2)\n131\t**Deliverables:** the definition-forging loop; the P3 example-space-stability predicate (ADVISORY-only); the example/monster regression suite; the autonomous emitter/abstain stub (formalize_status:requires-Phase-F); a D2 abstain fixture.\n132\t**Depends on:** DIALOGUE state machine\n133\t**done-when:** autonomous D2 never emits green; a forged-but-unfaithful but example-stable definition still stamps requires-Phase-F; P3 stability is advisory-only and never gates promotion.\n134\t- **Given** a forged definition that is example-stable but unfaithful, **when** autonomous D2 runs, **then** it stamps requires-Phase-F.\n135\t\n136\t## Wave 21 â€” Degradation-tripwire canary (A2 degradation-tripwire â€” global invariant)\n137\t**Deliverables:** the A2(degradation-tripwire) canary: delete the D1/D2 abstain fixtures â‡’ the system STILL refuses to emit green (the 1C runtime promote-gate), as a gated `node --test`.\n138\t**Depends on:** FORMALIZE Lakatosian loop\n139\t**done-when:** with the D1/D2 abstain fixtures deleted, the build still refuses any green/VERIFIED for proof/conceptual claims; the canary fails the build if a green would be emitted.\n140\t- **Given** the abstain fixtures deleted, **when** the degradation-tripwire canary runs, **then** the system still refuses green.\n141\t\n142\t## Wave 22 â€” CONTEXTUALIZE relation-classifier + commission canary (D3)\n143\t**Deliverables:** the native math relation classifier {generalization|specialization|equivalence|instance|structural-analogy}; every connection a CONCEPTUAL claim routed to A3; the commission canary.\n144\t**Depends on:** Degradation-tripwire canary\n145\t**done-when:** each proposed connection is emitted as a CONCEPTUAL claim routed to VERIFY (never settled by analogy); the commission canary holds.\n146\t- **Given** a proposed structural analogy, **when** D3 runs, **then** it is emitted as a CONCEPTUAL claim routed to VERIFY (not settled).\n147\t\n148\t## Wave 23 â€” Autonomous orchestrator + no-dispatch canary (D4)\n149\t**Deliverables:** user-explicit dispatch + an ADVISORY classifier, fail-safe ASK, read-only multi-pillar routing (grows the Wave-14 shim); the A2(no-dispatch) canary, regression-bound to the Wave-14 shim path.\n150\t**Depends on:** CONTEXTUALIZE relation-classifier + commission canary\n151\t**done-when:** the orchestrator routes read-only; the no-dispatch canary proves it cannot settle or commission-dispatch a verdict (no commission-id, no rung-flip) on ANY orchestrator OR Wave-14 shim path.\n152\t- **Given** an attempt by the orchestrator (or the shim) to emit a commission-id or flip a rung, **when** the no-dispatch canary runs, **then** the build fails.\n153\t\n154\t## Wave 24 â€” Gradeable oracle, part A: fixture corpus + red-team set (E1a)\n155\t**Deliverables:** the autonomous-tier fixtures (the iâ€“xiv union: the 6 planted-defect classes Ã— â‰¥3 instances + the FIXED 6-fixture SOUND subset + the ref-fn-independence fixture + the A4 laundering/recall rosters + the forged-unfaithful-definition fixture + the abstain-payload fixture + a RED-TEAM set incl. forged-artifact, cross-claim replay, same-claim replay, across-restart replay AND crash-mid-mint attempts).\n156\t**Depends on:** Autonomous orchestrator + no-dispatch canary\n157\t**done-when:** the corpus loads, each fixture is labeled with its class + expected verdict, and the red-team forged-artifact / cross-claim / same-claim / across-restart replay / crash-mid-mint attempts are each present and individually asserted as MUST-reject.\n158\t- **Given** the red-team set, **when** E1a's assertions run, **then** the forged-artifact, cross-claim, same-claim, across-restart replay, and crash-mid-mint fixtures are each rejected by the spine.\n159\t\n160\t## Wave 25 â€” Gradeable oracle, part B: Metric-G scorer + canned baseline + ablation (E1b)\n161\t**Deliverables:** the deterministic SCORER computing **Metric G = catch-rate âˆ’ false-positive-rate** over the **SCORED SUBSET** (the canonical token, used identically here and in DESCRIPTION Â§Residuals: the planted-defect computational/firewall fixtures; the FIXED 6-fixture SOUND subset is EXCLUDED from the catch-rate denominator and supplies ONLY the false-positive-rate / kâ€² term); the PINNED canned baseline (two stub scorers: always-ABSTAIN AND always-FLAG, scored on the SCORED SUBSET, G computed identically); the ABLATION arm.\n162\t**Depends on:** Gradeable oracle, part A: fixture corpus + red-team set\n163\t**done-when (cites the pinned constants):** **G(battery-on) > G(better-stub-baseline) + 0.30 (strict)** AND the ablation arm scores measurably lower; **per-class catch floors met** â€” derivation/dimensional/off-by-one = 100%, convergence-stability/comprehension-narrative/firewall-inapplicable â‰¥ 2/3 each; **kâ€² = at most 1 false positive on the FIXED 6-fixture SOUND subset**; **ABSTAIN-correctness = 100%** of proof/conceptual arms ABSTAIN.\n164\t- **Given** the ablation arm (battery disabled), **when** the scorer runs on the SCORED SUBSET, **then** G drops below battery-on by more than 0.30 (battery is load-bearing).\n165\t- **Given** either stub baseline, **when** the scorer runs, **then** battery-on G exceeds the better stub's G by > 0.30, and all per-class floors + kâ€² + the 100% abstain floor hold (else the wave HALTs).\n166\t\n167\t## Wave 26 â€” Journal integration (E2)\n168\t**Deliverables:** the 7-field journal schema + the sleep-loop input feeding the oracle's fixture-failure learning.\n169\t**Depends on:** Gradeable oracle, part B: Metric-G scorer + canned baseline + ablation\n170\t**done-when:** a run appends a 7-field journal entry and the sleep-loop consumes it (tested).\n171\t- **Given** a completed run, **when** journal integration executes, **then** a well-formed 7-field entry is appended and the sleep-loop reads it.\n172\t\n173\t## Wave 27 â€” Author SKILL.md (full) + invocation smoke test (E3) â€” project-DONE\n174\t**Deliverables:*